<title>UK: Kuwait, Saudi tell OPEC they at quota.</title>
<headline>Kuwait, Saudi tell OPEC they at quota.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia and Kuwait, two of OPEC's largest oil producers, told the group's Secretariat they produced at their quotas in October, the OPEC News Agency said.</p>
<p>They were among the first of the 11 OPEC members to provide their official wellhead production and market supply figures for October.</p>
<p>Data for the month of October received so far by the OPEC Secretariat from member countries is as follows(in 1,000 bpd):</p>
<p> Country	Production     Supply</p>
<p> Indonesia     1,325.6	    N/A</p>
<p> Kuwait	  2,002.4	    N/A</p>
<p> Libya	   1,400.0	    N/A</p>
<p> Qatar	     386.2	    N/A</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia  8,022.6	8,003.5</p>
<p> N/A - NOT AVAILABLE</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
